//
// RTL sources of the CVA6 Intel/Altera FPGA top level (`cva6_altera`), read
// by the `quartus-fpga-build` recipe through
// `config/target/<target>/Flist.cva6_altera`.
//
// Self-contained, like its Xilinx counterpart and for the same reason: the
// FPGA build substitutes core files by FPGA specific ones declaring the very
// same modules, and a filelist can add but not subtract. See the header of
// `corev_apu/fpga/Flist.cva6_fpga` for the details.
//
// On top of the Xilinx exclusions, the Altera build also drops the Xilinx
// top level and the JTAG TAP of the debug module: `cva6_altera.sv` is the top
// here, and the vJTAG bridge of `corev_apu/altera/src/` replaces
// `dmi_jtag*.sv` (the `altera_filter` of the root Makefile).
//
// The zero stage bootloader (`bootrom_<XLEN>.sv`) is NOT listed: it is
// generated by `fpga-bootrom` and added to the project from its build
// directory.
//
// Order matters: packages first, then the design. It reproduces the order the
// root Makefile fed Quartus with.

